From b3990e98f997e2b6f4b651e2f8e2e8f29b50ddf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Review <review@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:22:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] tu/mesh: Size chunk tables per pipeline and advertise
 what they cover

Indirect, indirect count and task draws launch their workgroups through
chunk arguments written by the setup shader. Only TU_MESH_MAX_CHUNKS (32)
mesh and TU_MESH_MAX_TASK_CHUNKS (4) task chunks existed, so any workgroups
past 32 * chunk_workgroups (resp. 4 * chunk_workgroups) were dropped without
an error, while maxMeshWorkGroupTotalCount and maxTaskWorkGroupTotalCount
were advertised as 1 << 22.

- Make the number of chunks a per-pipeline value (tu_mesh_state::num_chunks)
  derived from the advertised totals and the record or payload size, never
  below the old counts, and raise the table maximum to 256 / 32.
- The setup shader ran one thread per chunk in a 128 thread workgroup, so
  chunks 128 and up would never have been written. Loop over them.
- Advertise 1 << 16 mesh and 1 << 14 task workgroups per launch, which every
  shader within the advertised output limits can cover.
- Task pipelines get all mesh chunks, since one task chunk emits many mesh
  workgroups.

This does not remove truncation for amplification beyond the table
capacity (many task workgroups emitting many mesh workgroups, or an
indirect count draw whose commands sum to more than the capacity); that
needs GPU-side looping or per-task-chunk splitting. The limits are lower
than the 1 << 22 the Vulkan spec may require as a minimum for
VK_EXT_mesh_shader (not verified here).
